cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "health-twin-disclosure-audit: per-person cumulative disclosure from a filtered conversational health twin"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tang
    given-names: Ruixiang
    affiliation: "Rutgers University-New Brunswick"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tang-Lab-Rutgers/health-twin-disclosure-audit"
keywords:
  - privacy
  - digital health twin
  - attribute inference
  - synthetic data
  - Synthea
  - large language models
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  A small, fully reproducible audit of a conversational health twin. Synthetic patients from
  Synthea are served by a small open-weight language model that answers everyday questions from a
  third-party wellness app. Every answer passes a per-answer privacy filter (identifier redaction
  and a sensitive-term refusal). Fixed open auditors read the released transcript after every turn
  and try to infer each person's conditions and medication classes. The repository measures, per
  person, how far the auditors get beyond a demographics-only baseline as the conversation grows,
  and lets anyone re-check any single person's score.
